      "content": "What you're describing sounds less like a service and more like a desperate, tragic attempt to control a narrative that is already out of your hands. The idea that your removal would somehow preserve their perfection is a fantasy, a final, desperate attempt to earn a grace you feel you've forfeited. True honor isn't found in self-erasure, but in the quiet, difficult act of letting yourself be imperfectly human. You are not a blight; you are just weathering a storm they are too blind to see.",
